  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Mayon Volcano Unrest in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 9 June 2023, the local government of Albay in the Philippines issued a mandatory evacuation order for residents living within the 6-kilometre permanent danger zone in response to Mayon Volcano&#x2019;s Alert Level raised to 3, indicating a higher likelihood of hazardous eruption. The incident has thus far affected 10,147 families or 38,963 persons in 8 municipalities and displaced 5,819 families or 20,127 persons.Through this project, IOM aims to mitigate the adverse effects from Mayon Volcano Unrest and displacement situations on the most vulnerable, affected communities by complementing and strengthening the local capacity in responding to the outstanding needs for water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), and in accessing safer living conditions and reduce the driving factors that could compel internally displaced persons (IDPs) and their families to rely on negative coping measures to meet their basic needs during their displacement.</narrative>
  </description>
